Sure, if you that's all you do.  If you have a real system with lots
of programs, this philosophy quickly gets evil.  DOS limits the length
of the PATH variable, and quite a few things break if you have one
that is too long.  Leave the PATH alone and use a .bat file.
I never change my path when I install new programs.  (Of course I
use a real command interpreter, 4DOS, which gives me aliases)  If
you're using Windows, why not use a .pif file?  Or aren't there
hackers playing nethack anymore?

